# Iterate: one drawing, improved in place. Each beat is one ask, then the one or two lines that answer it; everything else
# on the stage is left exactly as it was. The boat is a group measured from its own waterline, so the last ask moves it
# whole with one line and no part can drift. The narration is one line said again under one id, so it never piles up.

look paper
scene boat figure canvas=square lines=1
line sea 4,72 96,72 thick=1
circle sun 84,13 6 fill=#f2b632 stroke=none
group boat at=32,74
poly hull in=boat -18,-10 18,-10 12,0 -12,0 fill=ink
rect mast in=boat -1,-50 2x40 fill=ink
say step | "Draw a boat." A hull and a mast: a first draft.
wait 1.5s
say step | "Give it a sail." Only the sail is drawn.
poly sail in=boat 1,-36 1,-14 13,-14 fill=accent
wait 2.5s
say step | "Make it bigger." The same sail grows where it stands.
poly sail in=boat 1,-42 1,-14 17,-14 fill=accent
wait 2.5s
say step | "Blue, and add a flag." One line recolours the sail, one more adds the flag.
set sail fill=alt
poly flag in=boat 1,-50 1,-44 9,-47 fill=accent
wait 2.5s
say step | "Now set sail." One line moves the whole boat: its parts are one group.
move boat 68,74 over=2s
wait 4s
